🔹 Demand for real-time screen sharing—a *massive* privacy and security violation, never required in legitimate investigations;  
🔹 Requests for IMEI number and ID scans *before any in-person verification*—this is classic identity theft bait;  
🔹 Threats of detention and account freezing within 12 hours—real law enforcement *never* issue ultimatums via text, and Article 191 procedures require formal written summons, not SMS;  
🔹 The email address `case.xmpsb_fcd@investigation.cn` is not an official government domain—authentic PRC agencies use `@xm.gov.cn`, `@fj.ps.gov.cn`, or `@police.cn`.

